Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
Upstream-Name: glitchvape
Upstream-Contact: Kamil J. Dudek <kamilek@localhost.localdomain>
Source: https://github.com/kamiljdudek/glitchvape-vibecoded
Comment:
 The program is MIT. Everything else here is a typeface that came with the
 source, and each is under whatever its author released it under -- which is
 not the same licence for any two of them, and in one case is not a licence
 document at all but the author's answer to the question.
 .
 GlitchVape does not paraphrase any of them. The file each author shipped is
 installed beside the font it covers, and `glitchvape --licenses` and the
 about window read those files off disk rather than quoting a copy pasted
 into Perl. The stanzas below say where each one came from.
 .
 W95FA is the exception and is why glitchvape-fonts-extra exists. See the
 stanza for it, and README.Debian.
Files-Excluded-Comment:
 Uncommenting the line below repacks the upstream tarball without the font
 whose terms are unverified, which is what an upload to Debian proper would
 need -- a source package in main may not carry it. It is left commented
 because it also removes the only thing glitchvape-fonts-extra installs.
 See README.Debian.
 .
 Files-Excluded: assets/fonts-nonfree

Files: *
Copyright: 2026 Kamil J. Dudek <kamilek@localhost.localdomain>
License: Expat

Files: debian/*
Copyright: 2026 Kamil J. Dudek <kamilek@localhost.localdomain>
License: Expat

Files: assets/fonts/DepartureMono-1.500/*
Copyright: 2024 Helena Zhang
License: OFL-1.1
Comment:
 https://departuremono.com/ -- the release is installed as published, with
 the author's LICENSE and README beside the font, which is what the OFL asks
 for.

Files: assets/fonts/fusion-pixel-font-12px-monospaced-otf-v2026.08.11/*
Copyright: TakWolf and the Fusion Pixel Font contributors
License: OFL-1.1
Comment:
 https://github.com/TakWolf/fusion-pixel-font -- a composite of several
 pixel fonts, each under its own copy of the OFL. The release carries a
 LICENSES/ directory with one per component and an OFL.txt for the whole;
 all of them are installed.

Files: assets/fonts/VCROSD/*
Copyright: 2015 Riciery Leal
License: LicenseRef-VCR-OSD-Mono
Comment:
 There is no licence document for this font. What there is instead is the
 author answering the question directly in the font's own comment thread at
 https://www.dafont.com/font-comment.php?file=vcr_osd_mono :
 .
 "mrmanet, author of VCR OSD Mono, Feb 24, 2017: Yes, the font is free even
 for commercial purposes."
 .
 That is an unconditional grant, and it is what assets/fonts/VCROSD/LICENSE
 records. It has no SPDX identifier, so it is named as a LicenseRef rather
 than being filed under a licence it is not.

Files: assets/fonts-nonfree/W95FA/*
Copyright: unknown
License: LicenseRef-Unverified
Comment:
 Packaged in glitchvape-fonts-extra and in nothing else. dafont lists this
 font as SIL Open Font License and as free for personal and commercial use,
 but the download carries no licence text and no statement by the author has
 been found that can be cited. A font aggregator's summary of terms is not
 the terms, so this is not filed as OFL-1.1: doing so would assert a licence
 whose text nobody here has seen.
 .
 assets/fonts-nonfree/W95FA/LICENSE records what is known and what would
 settle it.

